  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 substantially outperforms PCA n2000 in the RNA-only multi-profile setting (0.650 vs 0.591, config_005 vs config_002), and the best multimodal config so far (config_018: PCA, multi, avgpool, concat, ResNet50) achieves 0.619. Question: Does the scvi_n200 encoder improvement transfer to the multimodal setting? config_030 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 relative to config_018 (keeping multi-profile, avgpool, concat, ResNet50), cleanly isolating the encoder effect in the multimodal context. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly exploits the strongest single finding (scvi > PCA) in the most promising model architecture, uses a single-variable change to maintain interpretability, and if it succeeds, establishes scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder for further exploration (e.g., with ViT or transformer aggregation). If it fails, it tells us the scvi benefit is specific to RNA-only and the image modality interacts differently with the learned representation."
}

